(forall ((v Vehicle) (v_other Vehicle) (r Roadway) (t Int))
  (=> (and (on_roadway v r t)
           (on_roadway v_other r t)
           (not (= v v_other))
           (obstruction_present v r t)
           (crossing_center_line v r t)
           (approaching_opposite v_other v t)
           (in_authorized_lane v_other t)
           (not (obstruction_present v_other r t)))
      (yield_right_of_way_to_pedestrian v t)))

SCHEMA_INSUFFICIENT: The schema lacks a general `yield_right_of_way (Vehicle Vehicle Int) Bool` predicate for yielding to another vehicle. The only yield predicate is `yield_right_of_way_to_pedestrian` which is semantically incorrect for vehicle-to-vehicle yielding. Additionally, `is_immediate_hazard` requires an Intersection parameter, but the rule describes an immediate hazard between two vehicles on a roadway without any intersection context. A predicate like `is_immediate_hazard_vehicle (Vehicle Vehicle Int) Bool` (without Intersection) is needed.

